Provenance: tests/fixtures/astra_tiny/
============================================
Generated by tracks scripts on the astrasim-manal branch with the FIXED
Chakra writer (GlobalMetadata first, NodeType per et_def.proto, data_deps in
field 5, duration in field 7, uint64 comm_type/comm_size + bool-list
involved_dim attrs) and verified through the real AstraSim_BookSim2 binary:

  workload : 3 nodes (comp -> 1KB ring allreduce -> comp), 16 ranks, shared
  configs  : 16-node mesh4x4 (dor), ring collectives, 1 logical dim
  observed : rc=0 in ~0.2s wall, sys[0] finished at 50310 cycles with
             nonzero exposed communication

Do NOT regenerate by hand. If these fixtures ever need rebuilding, use the
fixed generate_chakra_trace.py and re-verify (rc=0, cycles>0) before
committing. Tests assert cycles>0 (not exact equality): subnetwork
assignment has a random component, so absolute cycles may vary run to run.

Files: one-coll.et (+ .0.et … .15.et per-rank copies), system.json,
network.json (relative booksim-config-file, exercising the JSON-unwrap +
relative-resolution path), logical_topology.json, memory.json, mesh4x4.cfg
(note: mesh4x4.cfg keeps standalone-style injection_rate=0.1, deliberately
exercising the CLI's injection_rate=0.0 embedded override).
